.TH "MIRU\-DAEMON" "1" "2026\-08\-07" "miru\-daemon Manual" "Miru"
.PP
.SH NAME
.PP
\fImiru\-daemon\fR \- Wayland\-native zooming daemon
.PP
.SH USAGE
.PP
To use \fImiru\-daemon\fR, you need to use \fImiructl\fR(1).\& 
.PP
miructl exposes the toggle/quit commands which toggle the daemon to take a screenshot of the current screen state and overlay it over the current screen and quit to quit the zoom mode.\&
.PP
You can also put the daemon in you systemctl service files to make it run on startup.\&
.PP
.PP
.SH Environment Variables 
.PP
\fImiru\-daemon\fR allows the usage of one environment variable \fBMIRU_DEBUG\fR which is to be set 0 or 1 to use \fImiru\-daemon\fR in debug mode or in normal mode.\& 
.PP
\fBMIRU_DEBUG=1\fR gives more detailed and verbose logs and \fBMIRU_DEBUG=0\fR gives the normal logs.\&
.PP
.PP
.SH Config file
.PP
\fImiru\-daemon\fR has a config file to configure \fImiru\-daemon\fR as you see fit.\& 
.PP
The config file is present at $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/miru/config.\&toml.\& 
.PP
In case $XDG_CONFIG_HOME is not set, it is present at $HOME/.\&config/miru/config.\&toml
.PP
See:
https://codeberg.\&org/Vaishnav\-Sabari\-Girish/miru#configuration
.PP
.PP
.SH Setting up a keybind
.PP
\fImiru\-daemon\fR can be toggled using a compositor\-level keybind (Niri, Hyprland, MangoWM etc) and pressing that keybind should rum miructl toggle
.PP
See:
https://codeberg.\&org/Vaishnav\-Sabari\-Girish/miru#setting\-up\-a\-keybind
.PP
.SH See also 
.PP
\fImiructl\fR(1)
.PP
